**Testing and Results**

| Check | Steps and test data | Expected result | Actual result | Status |
| ----- | ----- | ----- | ----- | ----- |
| 1\. Create | As user, submit “Event Creation Test” and details | Request saves, confirmation shows its title | When all necessary information was filled, success message shows. | Pass |
| 2\. Read and related tables | As staff, open Read | Saved request appears with correct user name and details | Results were filtered to find the request easier: the request was found. The information was correct. | Pass |
| 3\. Update | As staff, change \#54 to “Submitted” and reload | Status remains “Submitted” after reload | Status goes from “needs follow up” to “submitted”. Page keeps the saved change upon refresh. | Pass |
| 4\. Filter | Filter by In progress, completed, and All | Matching records only, correct empty message, All shows entire list again | Results were all marked with in-progress. Filtering by completed showed the correcte empty message, and All Statuses returned every entry. | Pass |
| 5\. Invalid input | As user, send direct create request with blank title using the console | Server rejects it, no new record created | Server rejected, sent error 400 message “Event name is required.” No request saved. | Pass |
| 6\. Protected access | While signed out, send an update request for \#57 using the console | Server rejects it, \#57 unchanged | Server rejects PATCH, 403 error. “Only Wellspring staff can do this” message in console. No “Update” button is allowed for clients. | Pass |
| 7\. Usability | A classmate attempts to schedule an event and confirm that it saved with the correct room as submitted. | Completes the task without help | Attempt was successful overall with some issues; Difficulties with adding multiple options under “technology” and “furniture”, no page refresh or new page shown upon submission, and “notes” in the database is on a second line all by itself, which makes it hard to see.  | Pass |

**Usability Observations (Task 7):**

* **Participant**  
  * Classmate from another team  
* **Task given:**  
  * Create an event request, check if it saved properly  
* **Whether they completed:**  
  * Completed  
* **Where they hesitated or became confused:**  
  * Selecting multiple options for “technology” and “furniture” and finding her saved submission (tester suggested user should be sent to requested events page upon submission)  
* **Help provided:**  
  * N/A

Improvement and Retest:

| Finding | Change made | Retest and actual result |
| ----- | ----- | ----- |
| The current system with showing the database is not effective, as the user needs to select a button to see the database, which is confusing and unclear. Also, users expected to be able to see their newly created event but were unable to. | Changed the default page view for the database to always show, and remove the “Show Database” button, and redirected users to the main page to receive their feedback.  | The test was creating a new event and seeing how the feedback works. The database is now always shown, without the “Show Database” button, and users are redirected to the main page to receive their feedback. The system works as expected. |

**Remaining Issues:**

* Staff cannot create entries and can only update status, priority, coordinator, and room.  
  * This still allows staff to work with the site and manage events, but in some scenarios they would not be able to manage events effectively.   
* Staff can only edit one entry at a time.  
  * This can slow down the overall workflow of staff but helps to ensure that errors do not damage events as much.  
* A click on “see event requests” is required to view entries of events, and clicking “Read” is necessary to see filters  
  * This can be confusing for users and is a poor workflow for User Experience.  
* New clients can create an account on the sign-in page. Staff roles are assigned only through 03\_auth.sql; there is no account-management screen, and accounts do not need email verification.  
  * This allows for security risks and false records through people creating fake accounts. Also, this makes managing which accounts get the staff role difficult.   
* There are no email notifications for creating an event.  
  * Users can be uncertain if their event was created, and has to go back to the dashboard to even check.    
* Room overlap is enforced by the database only for events with status “scheduled”.  
  * This can cause numerous issues for staff  as they manage events inside of Wellspring if there is overlap times scheduled.

